{
  "program": "CBACT04C",
  "caseId": "case01",
  "description": "The untouched-fixture baseline, and the case that fixes what a run over real production data actually does. TCATBALF row 0 of app/data/ASCII/tcatbal.txt is account 1, type 01, category 0001 with TRAN-CAT-BAL 0000000000{ - a positive zero, which every one of that fixture's fifty rows carries - and ACCTFILE row 0 of acctdata.txt is account 1 with ACCT-GROUP-ID as TEN SPACES, A000000000 sitting in ACCT-ADDR-ZIP at offset 103 instead. So MOVE ACCT-GROUP-ID TO FD-DIS-ACCT-GROUP-ID at :210 moves spaces, the READ at :416 reports '23', :418-419 display both disclosure-group lines, and :437-438 retry with 'DEFAULT   ' and hit. DIS-INT-RATE is then 15.00, so the guard at :214 is true and 1300-COMPUTE-INTEREST runs: 0.00 at 15.00 is 0.00, which is still WRITTEN - a zero-amount transaction is a transaction. The account is never rewritten, because the ELSE at :219-221 that would flush the last group's accumulated interest is unreachable, so ACCTFILE comes back byte-identical to its seed.",
